// Title: WMI Backdoor Exchange Transport Agent
// Sigma ID: 797011dc-44f4-4e6f-9f10-a8ceefbe566b
// Status: test | Level: critical
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2019-10-11 | Modified: 2023-02-08
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, T1546.003
// Description: Detects a WMI backdoor in Exchange Transport Agents via WMI event filters
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/cglyer/status/1182389676876980224
//   - https://twitter.com/cglyer/status/1182391019633029120
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_wmi_backdoor_exchange_transport_agent.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\EdgeTransport.exe" and (not((FolderPath =~ "C:\\Windows\\System32\\conhost.exe" or (FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft\\Exchange Server\\" and FolderPath endswith "\\Bin\\OleConverter.exe"))))
